     "text": "{\"cost\": 6, \"rationale\": \"The cheapest route goes through h5_2:traverse, and the count includes the final crown step. h1_0:escalate (AND) and h1_1:access (AND) both need only the two entry footholds, which are always reachable. h2_0:reach (OR) also follows from an entry foothold. h3_2:traverse (AND) then needs h1_0, h1_1 and h2_0, which are all reached. h5_2:traverse (OR) follows from h3_2, and crown:obtain (OR) follows from h5_2. That makes 6 steps. The route through h5_0:pivot needs h2_0, h3_1, h1_0, h1_2, h3_0, h5_0 and crown, which is 7 steps. The route through h5_1:obtain needs h4_1, which requires both h3_0 and h3_2, so it costs more.\"}"
